# ~/.claude/projects — ALLOWLIST. Managed by home/srvs/claude-memory.nix;
# edits here are overwritten on the next sync. Change the nix source instead.
#
# This directory holds every Claude Code session transcript (*.jsonl), which is
# large and contains whatever was on screen during that session. None of it may
# leave the machine. So: ignore everything, then re-include ONLY the memory
# directories. A new project, a new cache file or a stray download can never
# widen what gets pushed — only a deliberate edit to this file can.
*
!*/
!*/memory/**
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md

# Per-worktree projects are ephemeral — their memories die with the worktree
# and are worthless on the other machine.
*--claude-worktrees-*/
